Dermoscopy shows a symmetric, round to oval lesion with homogeneous light to dark brown pigmentation, a regular pigment network or clustered globules, evenly distributed dots, smooth well-defined borders, and occasional peripheral fading or halo.
In dermoscopy a melanocytic nevus typically appears as a well-circumscribed brown to tan lesion with a regular pigment network, uniform globules or homogeneous areas, occasional peripheral rim, variable shades ranging from light brown to dark black.
often appears as a symmetric, round or oval lesion with a uniform light-to-dark brown pigment, regular reticular or globular patterns, well-defined smooth borders, occasional central hyperpigmentation or perifollicular hypopigmented areas.
a well-circumscribed oval lesion showing a symmetric reticular pigment network with evenly distributed small brown globules, homogeneous light-to-dark brown areas, occasional central darker blotch, peripheral fading, and sparse blue-gray speckling.
In dermoscopy a melanocytic nevus variation 5 often appears as a symmetric, well‑circumscribed brown to tan lesion with uniform pigment, regular pigment network or clustered globules, smooth borders, occasional central structureless areas, and variable dots.
Dermoscopy reveals a symmetric, well‑circumscribed lesion with uniform brown to tan pigmentation and regular pigment network, often with evenly distributed globules or dots, occasional peripheral fading, smooth borders, and rare focal blue‑gray or central darker hub.
shows a well‑circumscribed, symmetric brown to tan lesion with a regular pigment network or clustered globules, often with homogeneous structureless areas, occasional peripheral streaks and small dots, varying shades across the lesion.
dermoscopic image shows a well-circumscribed round to oval lesion with uniform light-to-dark brown pigmentation, regular pigment network or clustered globules, occasional blue-gray dots, smooth borders, and small perifollicular hypopigmented areas.
Dermoscopic melanocytic nevus appears as a well-circumscribed round or oval lesion with uniform light-to-dark brown pigmentation, regular reticular network or clustered globules, occasional homogeneous structureless areas and symmetrical distribution; variation 9 shows increased globularity.
often appears as a symmetric, round to oval lesion with uniform tan-to-dark brown coloration, a reticular or globular pigment network, smooth well-defined borders, occasional central hyperpigmentation and peripheral fading.
